we discuss an efficient numerical scheme for the recursive filtering of diffusive quantum stochastic master equations . We show (proof) the independence of the diffusion coefficients of the stochastic force and the diffusion term in such a state-dependent diffusive master equation. We obtain some analytical results that help to understand the asymptotic behaviour of our state-dependent filter. We then generalize our scheme to address the filtering of more complex state-dependent stochastic master equations.

The plan of this paper is the following. Section \[sec:stochastic\_difffree\] is dedicated to the mathematical framework for stochastic differential equations with random coefficients and state-dependent diffusive terms. Section \[sec:quantum\] contains our generalization to quantum systems. Section \[sec:numerical-discretization\] is dedicated to the numerical discretization. We address in particular the treatment of the diffusive terms and provide some analytical results about their asymptotic behaviour. In section \[subsec:filter\] we provide general results about the recursive filter. Section \[sec:examples\] is dedicated to a numerical experiment conducted on a specific model system.

