we study the dynamics of the `` kolkata paise restaurant problem '' . the problem is the following : in each period , @xmath0 agents have to choose between @xmath0 restaurants . agents have a common ranking of the restaurants . they go to a restaurant, @xmath0 and pay their favorite, where they are served the restaurant @xmath0 ; but they are refused at @xmath0, then they go to the @xmath1 restaurant and pay their second favorite in that same period. they are served @xmath1, but refused if the best restaurant has already been served. they continue in this way, they go to the third restaurant and pay their third favorite in the period they find out that the first two favorite restaurants have already been served. they leave the game when the last restaurant was chosen.

In this way a agent's ranking will vary depending on his memory (he will choose the restaurant with the highest paid at the beginning of the period).

